{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-139555-r4517192","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Pumpkin Bread III","sourcePageId":139555,"sourceRevision":"4517192","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-20T19:31:30Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Pumpkin%20Bread%20III&oldid=4517192","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:46:08.534Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baking recipes","Category:Breakfast recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Inexpensive recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for dessert","Category:Recipes for pumpkin bread","Category:Recipes using baking powder","Category:Recipes using baking soda","Category:Recipes using clove","Category:Recipes using cooking spray","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using granulated sugar","Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon","Category:Recipes using nutmeg","Category:Recipes using pumpkin","Category:Recipes using walnut","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Vegetarian recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"c0850c9402168dcf3e168dd61f2b8af7222b29b61d2a3b6a4a64ea7e51f3e5cf","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary|category=Cake recipes|yield=2 loaves|time=1 hour|difficulty=2}}{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of the United States|American cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Dessert|Dessert]]\n__NOTOC__\n''See also: [[Cookbook:Pumpkin bread|Pumpkin Bread]] and [[Cookbook:Pumpkin Bread II|Pumpkin Bread II]].''\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 1½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] white granulated [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:Oil|oil]]\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]], [[Cookbook:Beat|beaten]]\n* 1 can (15 [[Cookbook:Ounce|ounces]]) [[Cookbook:pumpkin|pumpkin purée]]\n* 3 cups [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n* ¾ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Baking Powder|baking powder]]\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Baking Soda|baking soda]]\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Clove|cloves]]\n* ½ teaspoon ground [[Cookbook:Nutmeg|nutmeg]]\n* ¾ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Chop|chopped]] [[Cookbook:Nut|nuts]]\n* [[Cookbook:Cooking Spray|Cooking spray]]\n\n==Procedure==\n# Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to [[Cookbook:Oven_temperatures|350°F]].\n# [[Cookbook:Beat|Beat]] sugar and oil using [[Cookbook:Mixer|electric hand mixer]].\n# Add eggs and pumpkin and beat lightly.\n# Add flour, then baking powder, baking soda, cinnamon, cloves, nutmeg, salt, and nuts if desired. Mix well.\n# Pour into two [[Cookbook:Pots and Pans|baking pans]] sprayed lightly with cooking spray.\n# [[Cookbook:Bake|Bake]] until [[Cookbook:Skewer|toothpick]] comes out clean from the center, about 40–45 minutes.\n# Cool and serve.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n* Chopped [[Cookbook:Walnut|walnuts]] are particularly good in this bread, but other nuts will do.\n* If cooking in a [[Cookbook:Dutch oven|Dutch oven]], preheat with about 14 charcoal briquettes, with about 10 or 11 on top and 3 or 4 on the bottom. If you're cooking outdoors, you'll have to use a hand mixer or a strong arm with the spoon.\n* If your bread sticks to the greased pan, try coating the greased pan with a thin layer of flour or a piece of [[Cookbook:Parchment Paper|parchment paper]].\n* If you want to use fresh cooked pumpkin instead of canned pumpkin, follow these directions:\n*# Cut the a small cooking/pie pumpkin into small section (that will fit into the pot you will use to cook them).\n*# Bring water to a boil in a large pot (enough water so the none of the pumpkin slices will be sitting on the bottom of the pot).\n*# Add pumpkin slices to the boiling water, cook for about 15 minutes or until pumpkin is soft.\n*# Remove pumpkin slices from water.\n*# Using a knife or spoon, peel/cut away the skin.\n*# The pumpkin can be used right away for cooking, or can be refrigerated/frozen until needed.\n\n[[Category:Inexpensive recipes]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for pumpkin bread]]\n[[Category:Breakfast recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using nutmeg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pumpkin]]\n[[Category:Recipes using walnut]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking soda]]\n[[Category:Recipes using granulated sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using clove]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cooking spray]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Pumpkin Bread III","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1½ cups white granulated sugar","sourceText":"1½ cups white granulated sugar","amountText":"1½ cups white granulated sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 cup oil","sourceText":"1 cup oil","amountText":"1 cup oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"3 eggs, beaten","sourceText":"3 eggs, beaten","amountText":"3 eggs, beaten","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 can (15 ounces) pumpkin purée","sourceText":"1 can (15 ounces) pumpkin purée","amountText":"1 can (15 ounces)